    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 green).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, validated, lower-cased owner `email` across the full request\u2192persistence\u2192response round trip.\n\n**Contract / DTO** \u2014 added `email` to the `OwnerFields` schema in `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (optional `string`, `format: email`). The OpenAPI generator produces the field on both `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response), and MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n\n**Persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java`: added the `email` field (`@Column(name = \"email\")`) with getter/setter.\n- Added an `email` column to all four `db/*/schema.sql` files.\n- Fixed the positional seed `INSERT`s in `db/hsqldb/data.sql` and `db/mysql/data.sql` (the h2/postgres seeds already use explicit column lists) \u2014 otherwise the extra column caused a \"row column count mismatch\" at startup.\n\n**Validation + normalization** (per the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions, not `@ControllerAdvice`)\n- `rest/escalation/InvalidEmailException.java` (checked, \u2192 400) + `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler.java` + the `officefloor/escalation/...InvalidEmailException.yml` mapping, mirroring the existing `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n- `rest/function/owner/OwnerEmail.java`: shared normalizer \u2014 null/blank \u21d2 `null`; otherwise trims, lower-cases, and rejects a syntactically invalid address with `InvalidEmailException`.\n- Wired it into `RequireOwnerFields` (the `POST /api/owners` entry step) and `ApplyOwner` (the `PUT /api/owners/{ownerId}` mutate step).\n\nThe three acceptance tests now pass: missing email is accepted, `Test.User@Example.COM` is stored/returned as `test.user@example.com`, and `not-an-email` yields 400.",
